                        "review": "Ok so my first journey kind of went as follows:\n\n-Jumped to first sector blasted some asteriods got 21 copper and 58 stone\n\n-Second sector was Alliance and I seen an oceanic world atmosphere extreme tried and lost shuttle and crew. Hung around and got an agricultural cruiser to give me 43 food and bulk carrier tried for fuel but he didnt want to talk\n\n-Third sector kind of empty but had a space staton it wanted 1439 docking fee, nope too expensive. I jumped out c-ya!\n\n-Fourth sector Lucicron got a cargo ship to give me food and another to give me supplies. Fighter group attacked me lost 20 hull and jumped out\n\n-Fifth sector desert world moderate atmosphere with locatons went down drove rover walked out and sand worm killed me!\n\n-Sixth sector nomads and space station. Docked for $55 not much here but a shipyard and bar & grill but lots of people. I got several energy packs from people and once nice enough to give me almost $200 gc. Found something in a couple lockers not sure what one was other was 12 luxury items. Went to shipyard and bought energy module and energy storage and departed\n\n-Seventh sector a few asteroids and some purple looking planet. Fighters started attacking me tried to shoot back couldnt hit. Got hit again and again, tried shields ran out of energy. Went to hit jump and boom! All over.\n\nSo yeah so far this game is pretty cool and theres a lot to do here. A bit challenging but gets easier once you get the hang of it. Seems like it has a lot of potential and I can't wait to see where it all goes. I noticed the developer seems very supportive and dedicated. Found a few issues but nothing too major. I will definitely be playing this one more!\n\n",
